        "display_name": null,
        "comment": "Mirai build served as tadashi.x64 from 13.140.176.180:8911. Sandboxed execution (simulated network, no tracer): C2 13.140.176.180:14593/tcp, hard-coded IP, connect every 10 s, no DNS. Under strace it never reaches the network: it respawns every ~13 s, renaming itself (cron/atd/rsyslogd/...), after reading its processes /proc/N/status (TracerPid) - likely anti-debug. Single instance via abstract unix socket @t_esi; Mirai-style /proc/*/exe killer. A string absent from the file on disk is decrypted at runtime: Tadashi Tv Control Unit only $24.99 brother, deal of a lifetime brother. Oh also fuck yall researchers. Operator context: Hunt.io xlabs_v1 report (https://hunt.io/blog/xlabs-v1-ddos-for-hire-operation-exposed). Related: 43efb4f01b17c9a2b9c52f926113493b0e896778e1f4d547ce20b00432d76f4c, 0e8870f48e3971b4f1586129a25be97ba15ff6fcca0b7abb303b7c02f1f94b85."
